WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:21.992
Mrs. Lynde, an old friend of Marilla's, had come to Green Gables to visit and discuss the latest town "news," though most people called it gossip.

2
00:00:21.993 --> 00:00:30.169
"I've heard that you started an improvement society, Anne. Is it true?" asked Mrs. Lynde.

3
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:40.210
"Not really," said Anne, flushing. "I was just talking it over with some friends. Many towns have improvement societies now."

4
00:00:40.211 --> 00:00:48.817
"It's not a good idea," said Mrs. Lynde. "People don't like being improved, Anne."

5
00:00:48.818 --> 00:00:52.523
"We're not improving the people," said Anne.

6
00:00:52.524 --> 00:01:00.298
"We want to make Avonlea prettier. For instance, we're thinking of painting the town hall."

7
00:01:00.299 --> 00:01:06.267
Mrs. Lynde was unconvinced, but soon the Avonlea Improvement Society was organized,

8
00:01:06.268 --> 00:01:15.533
with Gilbert Blythe as president, Fred Wright as vice-president, Anne Shirley as secretary, and Diana Barry as treasurer.

9
00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:23.363
The Improvement Society received some disapproval and a good deal of ridicule from Avonlea's older citizens.

10
00:01:23.364 --> 00:01:28.591
Mr. Wright said a better name for the Society would be the "Dating Club."

11
00:01:28.592 --> 00:01:36.504
Mr. Bell said that he might be willing to paint his barn, but there was no way he'd hang lace curtains in his stables.

12
00:01:36.505 --> 00:01:41.264
Despite these jokes the "Improvers" set to work.

13
00:01:41.265 --> 00:01:46.283
Anne and Diana walked along an Avonlea road, visiting each house.

14
00:01:46.284 --> 00:01:51.514
They were collecting donations for the Improvement Society to paint the town hall.

15
00:01:51.515 --> 00:01:56.513
Their first stop was the home of Catherine and Eliza Andrews.

16
00:01:56.514 --> 00:02:03.587
"If Catherine is here, we might get some money," said Diana, "but if Eliza is there, we won't."

17
00:02:03.588 --> 00:02:07.593
Eliza Andrews answered the door, looking very grim.

18
00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:11.837
As the girls explained their errand, Catherine came to the door.

19
00:02:11.838 --> 00:02:16.821
Eliza listened with a frown, but Catherine smiled.

20
00:02:16.822 --> 00:02:22.990
"I won't give any money for that hall, not a cent," said Eliza sourly.

21
00:02:22.991 --> 00:02:26.158
"It's just a place for young people to meet.

22
00:02:26.159 --> 00:02:31.388
Young people should stay at home. This world is getting worse every day!"

23
00:02:31.389 --> 00:02:36.217
"I think it's getting better!" said Catherine firmly.

24
00:02:36.218 --> 00:02:42.892
Eliza changed the subject. "How are Marilla's eyes, Anne? Is she blind yet?"

25
00:02:42.893 --> 00:02:47.375
"Her eyes aren't any worse," Anne replied meekly.

26
00:02:47.376 --> 00:02:54.384
Anne and Diana left disappointed, but as they headed down the road a woman ran up behind them.

27
00:02:54.385 --> 00:02:58.721
It was Catherine Andrews with a dollar in her hand.

28
00:02:58.722 --> 00:03:05.471
"Good luck with the Improvement Society!" she said. The girls cheered up.

29
00:03:05.472 --> 00:03:13.245
Their next visit was to Mrs. Bell, who looked very healthy but spent a half an hour describing all her aches and pains.

30
00:03:13.246 --> 00:03:21.114
Mrs. Bell gave them money but said she couldn't donate next year because she would probably be in her grave by then.

31
00:03:21.115 --> 00:03:23.837
The worst reception was at the Fletchers'.

32
00:03:23.838 --> 00:03:31.670
Anne and Diana saw two faces in the window as they walked up to the door, but when Anne knocked, nobody answered.

33
00:03:31.671 --> 00:03:36.003
Eventually the Improvers raised enough money to paint the hall.

34
00:03:36.004 --> 00:03:43.171
They decided on dark green and asked Mr. Joshua Pye, an uncle of Anthony Pye, to paint it.

35
00:03:43.172 --> 00:03:51.212
They had to give the contract to a member of the Pye family, or else none of the four Pye families would donate any money.

36
00:03:51.213 --> 00:03:58.424
Mr. Roger Pye brought the hall paint home that night, and Mr. Joshua Pye began painting the next day.

37
00:03:58.425 --> 00:04:01.679
He was not disturbed in his task.

38
00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:09.331
The hall was so closely surrounded by a wood of fir trees that it was invisible to anyone not driving right by it.

39
00:04:09.332 --> 00:04:15.078
Mr. Joshua Pye finished his job Friday afternoon and went home to Carmody.

40
00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:18.513
Later Mrs. Lynde drove by the hall.

41
00:04:18.514 --> 00:04:24.127
She was curious to see what the hall looked like in its new coat of paint.

42
00:04:24.128 --> 00:04:33.945
When Mrs. Lynde rounded the curve and saw the brilliant blue town hall, she dropped the reins and said, "Good gracious!"

43
00:04:33.946 --> 00:04:40.558
She stared for a moment and then laughed hysterically.

44
00:04:40.559 --> 00:04:44.308
News of the mistake quickly spread through Avonlea.

45
00:04:44.309 --> 00:04:55.173
"Oh, it's simply dreadful!" Anne exclaimed. "I just can't believe Joshua Pye has gone and painted the hall blue instead of green.

46
00:04:55.174 --> 00:04:59.848
It's the blue that people use to paint carts and wheelbarrows.

47
00:04:59.849 --> 00:05:05.874
And Mrs. Lynde says it's the most hideous color for a building that she's ever seen."

48
00:05:05.875 --> 00:05:10.324
"How on earth could such a mistake have happened?" asked Diana.

49
00:05:10.325 --> 00:05:14.944
The blame for this disaster was eventually pinned on the Pyes.

50
00:05:14.945 --> 00:05:18.696
The shades of paint were selected from a numbered color card.

51
00:05:18.697 --> 00:05:24.923
The Improvers had chosen the color number 147 and had told Roger Pye.

52
00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:31.496
However, Roger had somehow bought color number 157 instead.

53
00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:38.281
"I must cry, even if I am almost 17 years old, Marilla," Anne later sobbed.

54
00:05:38.282 --> 00:05:44.085
"It is so embarrassing—people will think the Improvement Society is a joke.

55
00:05:44.086 --> 00:05:49.263
They'll never again listen to our ideas or give us donations."

56
00:05:49.264 --> 00:05:55.041
In life, however, things often turn out differently from how we expect.

57
00:05:55.042 --> 00:05:59.993
The Avonlea people did not laugh at the Improvement Society.

58
00:05:59.994 --> 00:06:05.666
They had donated money to have the town hall painted, and they were angry about the mistake.

59
00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:13.736
Public indignation centered on the Pyes. People felt that Joshua Pye should have realized it was the wrong color.

60
00:06:13.737 --> 00:06:23.352
Joshua Pye argued that he painted the hall the color he was given, and it wasn't his job to question the Improvement Society's taste in color.

61
00:06:23.353 --> 00:06:30.207
Despite Joshua Pye's arguments, the people of Avonlea still took the Improvement Society's side.

62
00:06:30.208 --> 00:06:37.390
People believed the Improvers had worked hard, and many of them took inspiration from the Society's example.

63
00:06:37.391 --> 00:06:45.176
Mr. Major Spencer said he would plant flowers around the town, and Mr. Bell decided to paint his old barn.

64
00:06:45.177 --> 00:06:49.448
Anne, however, was still upset about the town hall.

65
00:06:49.449 --> 00:06:56.782
"Never mind, Anne," Marilla consoled her. "Most paint fades uglier over time.

66
00:06:56.783 --> 00:07:03.199
But that blue started out as ugly as it can be. So it's bound to fade prettier."

67
00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:13.861
Anne smiled, but she was not convinced.
